<body>
    <h1>Remote Management in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"6be118c92178">In IGEL OS, endpoint devices are manag=
ed using the Universal Management Suite (UMS). This article shows the setti=
ngs related to the remote management, for example, the configuration of UMS=
 servers and user information dialogs on UMS updates.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"dc4d7d2f436a">
<p local-id=3D"240236ca8eb0">Menu path: <strong>System &gt; Remote Manageme=
nt</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"3fb87f8e7801"></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wr=
apper image-left-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"con=
fluence-embedded-image confluence-content-image-border image-left" alt=3D"i=
mage-20240918-103035.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"8ce0f33471f=
8de4707be626888d08bab7951d0058049057167b75c4a19e7ca86" data-image-src=3D"ht=
tps://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302629/image-2024=
0918-103035.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1726655437397&amp;cacheV=
ersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"742" data-width=3D"1659" data-unres=
olved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"171573338" data-linked=
-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linke=
d-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20240918-103035.png" data-base-url=3D"htt=
ps://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"ima=
ge/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302629" data-linked-resource=
-container-version=3D"16" data-media-id=3D"b1d02457-9cae-4d62-a396-c2545db1=
6afd" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"209"></span>
<p local-id=3D"eeb8dd9cc634"></p>
<p local-id=3D"5979fa371c47"><strong>Universal Management Suite</strong></p=
>
<p local-id=3D"36cc39bf0b15">If the device is registered on a <strong>UMS S=
erver</strong>, its IP address / hostname and <strong>Port number</strong> =
will be shown in the list.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"4fad8662ef2d"><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=
=3D"6696cf5b-55a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5">The list can contain more than on=
e UMS instance. The device will go through the entries in the list until it=
 can contact a UMS Server successfully.</span></p>
<p local-id=3D"f8dd4f7f31e9"><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=
=3D"6696cf5b-55a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5"> Starting with IGEL OS 12.8.0, th=
e device will only use the DNS entry </span><code><span class=3D"inline-com=
ment-marker" data-ref=3D"6696cf5b-55a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5">igelrmserver=
</span></code><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"6696cf5b-55=
a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5"> during registration or as a fallback if no UMS =
addresses are configured or if contact to </span><code><span class=3D"inlin=
e-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"6696cf5b-55a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5">igelrms=
erver</span></code><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"6696cf=
5b-55a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5"> is explicitly enabled using the option </s=
pan><strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"6696cf5b-55a9=
-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5">System &gt; Remote Management &gt; Options &gt; Us=
e "igelrmserver" as fallback</span></strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-m=
arker" data-ref=3D"6696cf5b-55a9-46ee-ad7c-85189b3dc9e5">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"90067172730a"></p>
<p local-id=3D"016e3bc8f9e0">To manage the list of servers:</p>
<div class=3D"error">
<span class=3D"error">Unable to render {include}</span> The included page c=
ould not be found.
</div>
<p local-id=3D"103bca5dc7bd"></p>
<div class=3D"error">
<span class=3D"error">Unable to render {include}</span> The included page c=
ould not be found.
</div>
<ul local-id=3D"e3b36e847a89">
<li local-id=3D"6cedc7a687d7">
<p local-id=3D"07382b109866"><strong>UMS server</strong><br>
Name or IP of the UMS Server</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"69be3d418152">
<p local-id=3D"87622f6ec404"><strong>Port number</strong><br>
Port number of the UMS Server (Default: 8443)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a065d789ee58">
<p local-id=3D"6c94e4fd0d47"><strong>Connector type</strong><br>
The value is automatically defined by the UMS. You can use the <strong>Rank=
ing of connectors</strong> option under <strong>System &gt; Remote Manageme=
nt &gt; Options</strong> to define which connection the device should try t=
o establish first based on the connector types.<br>
Possible values:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f51b186c2619">
<li local-id=3D"ac95662676c7">
<p local-id=3D"73424aede6e2"><strong>undefined</strong> (default)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"66c2b645f81d">
<p local-id=3D"34638d37584d"><strong>ums</strong><br>
Direct connection to the Universal Management Suite.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"62fb7a3893be">
<p local-id=3D"737c7efa9eea"><strong>icg</strong><br>
Connection to the IGEL Cloud Gateway (ICG).</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"534c18d146c3"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"517b03c694c8"><strong>Display =E2=80=9CApply changes=E2=80=
=9D dialog on boot</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"1d0f1499aca3">If new settings were made in the UMS, the devi=
ce may receive them during the boot procedure.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"ad0fe46546aa">=E2=98=91&nbsp;During the boot procedure, the&=
nbsp;<strong>Apply changes</strong>&nbsp;dialog is displayed and the user c=
an decide whether the reconfiguration process runs immediately. (Default)</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"ed8b526801e0">=E2=98=90&nbsp;The <strong>Apply changes</stro=
ng> dialog will not be shown. The new settings will be applied or ignored d=
epending on the setting under&nbsp;<strong>Default action on boot</strong>.=
</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"9d25dc20047c">With the <strong>Apply changes</strong> dialog=
 the user can only control when the reconfiguration process runs. If the us=
er refuses the reconfiguration process, it is delayed till the next system =
restart. Even if the user refuses the reconfiguration, parameter values are=
 always applied.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"b39b5670e53f"></p>
<p local-id=3D"27ce482cf83e"><strong>Timeout</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"080a53e8250d">Number of seconds for which the&nbsp;<strong>A=
pply changes</strong>&nbsp;dialog is shown.&nbsp;If the timeout is exceeded=
, the received settings will automatically be applied. (Default:&nbsp;20)<b=
r>
Setting the value to 0 disables the timeout, and the dialog is shown until =
the user clicks a button.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4925d6f0a2e2"></p>
<p local-id=3D"d34a3e36995f"><strong>Default action on boot</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"53cf72b00121">Configure the action that is to be performed i=
f the dialog exceeds the timeout or if the timeout is disabled.<br>
Possible values:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"84d450b39b78">
<li local-id=3D"d5bb20db34b1">
<p local-id=3D"2d8783f1e364"><strong>Apply changed configuration immediatel=
y</strong>: New settings will take effect immediately, and programs that ar=
e running may be restarted. (Default)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"99d4f26b3d41">
<p local-id=3D"cfb7803efb75"><strong>Ignore changed configuration</strong>:=
 New settings will not be applied. The new configuration will be saved on t=
he device, and applied the next time a new configuration is applied.</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"3271acdc2d60"></p>
<p local-id=3D"b5bdfccfd58b"><strong>Prompt user on UMS actions</strong></p=
>
<p local-id=3D"90acc5e8d9e6">=E2=98=91 The user is informed through a messa=
ge window when UMS actions are performed on the device. (Default)</p><span =
class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper confluence-emb=
edded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-conte=
nt-image-border image-left" width=3D"400" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"3708d29c7=
25bbcd1cccee858a00b685a7c42e3ccd2d8d0a8a4cafbf8f7a27f7e" data-image-src=3D"=
https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302629/OS12_Rem=
ote_mgm_Userinfo.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364681565&amp;c=
acheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"199" data-width=3D"500" data-u=
nresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73308931" data-lin=
ked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-li=
nked-resource-default-alias=3D"OS12_Remote_mgm_Userinfo.png" data-base-url=
=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302629" data-linked-r=
esource-container-version=3D"16" data-media-id=3D"9f3a3b27-3a7d-4972-8d87-a=
0d6caa833bb" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"159"></span>
<p local-id=3D"84673d9af55f">=E2=98=90 The user is not informed when UMS ac=
tions are performed on the device.</p>
<p local-id=3D"dcde89674ce5"></p>
<p local-id=3D"831af9561733"><strong>Timeout</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"661857e38c70">Number of seconds for which the UMS actions&nb=
sp;information dialog is shown.&nbsp;If the timeout is exceeded, the receiv=
ed settings will automatically be applied. (Default:&nbsp;20)<br>
Setting the value to 0 disables the timeout, and the dialog is shown until =
the user clicks on a button.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c6d2f89133f6"></p>
<p local-id=3D"08a0f3053725"><strong>Structure tag</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"3a7f51c1d77f">The structure tag is used to sort the device i=
nto a directory in accordance with the UMS directory rules. For details see=
 <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENLITEUMSP/pages/20=
2117359" data-linked-resource-id=3D"202117359" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"3" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">/wiki/spaces/ENLITEUMSP/pages/202=
117359</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"4a4c849b5d16">Instead of setting the structure tag using thi=
s option, the preferable way to manually set the structure tag in the OS12 =
is using the command tool: <code>/sbin/rmagent-set-structure-tag -t &lt;TAG=
&gt;</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"28e3281a7e9b">Instead of checking the structure tag here, us=
e the command tool <code>/sbin/rmagent-get-structure-tag</code> for retriev=
ing of the current value of the structure tag in the OS12. Because if the s=
tructure tag is set via Setup Assistant or via DHCP tag, the value in the S=
etup will be empty, but the command will always retrieve the value.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-tip=
">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-approve confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"674a00d662b6">The command line tool <code>/sbin/rmagent-regi=
ster</code> provides the possibility to set the structure tag using the opt=
ion <code>-u &lt;TAG&gt;</code>. This tool is used for some scenarios of au=
tomatic register with custom scripts.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"89a68e28cc53"></p>
<p local-id=3D"b435f29ab7f7"><strong>Log message severity</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"f32bb1d22f97">Select the severity level above which device e=
rrors are to be transferred to the UMS. Messages with a lower severity are =
suppressed.<br>
Possible options:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a6e5c874dcc8">
<li local-id=3D"07055f1274c1">
<p local-id=3D"d16d2549b530"><strong>off</strong> (Default)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ce1934efd581">
<p local-id=3D"be009befd1d6"><strong>error</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"360b22d4c2d1">
<p local-id=3D"3754692cb2db"><strong>warn</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"efea0201bb6e">
<p local-id=3D"8f71224eb964"><strong>info</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"21b8f435cc70">
<p local-id=3D"0542a5ed9aca"><strong>debug</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"703b0d378c55"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c5c944073b59"><strong>Show UMS connection status tray icon o=
n desktop</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"d00330d559bd">=E2=98=91 The <span class=3D"confluence-embedd=
ed-file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-content=
-image-inline" alt=3D"image-20240716-123133.png" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"df=
5af5549ab12caa1110c59e39387fa3e83c21135571942a12e50636f32175e9" data-image-=
src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302629/i=
mage-20240716-123133.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1721133094770&a=
mp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"44" data-width=3D"44" data=
-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"121472135" data-=
linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data=
-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20240716-123133.png" data-base-url=
=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302629" data-linked-r=
esource-container-version=3D"16" data-media-id=3D"e28e4cf5-c6fb-4dfb-be09-5=
93e86ffb266" data-media-type=3D"file" width=3D"44" height=3D"44"></span> ic=
on is displayed in the taskbar, showing the status of the UMS connection. C=
licking the icon displays information about the connected UMS server.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a0990d7e1233"><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
